\title{geotessera: read Tessera embeddings from Zarr stores}
\description{
Tessera is a foundation model for Earth observation that summarises a
year of Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 observations as an embedding at each
10 m pixel. This package reads published embeddings from Zarr stores.
}
\details{
Open a store with \code{\link[=tessera_open]{tessera_open()}}, by default the v1.1 global dClimate
run; \code{\link[=tessera_datasets]{tessera_datasets()}} lists the others. Then:
\itemize{
\item sample points with \code{\link[=tessera_sample]{tessera_sample()}} or \code{\link[=tessera_probe]{tessera_probe()}};
\item read a region with \code{\link[=tessera_region]{tessera_region()}} or \code{\link[=tessera_map_region]{tessera_map_region()}};
\item read a fixed-size patch with \code{\link[=tessera_patch]{tessera_patch()}};
\item write GeoTIFF files with \code{\link[=tessera_export_geotiffs]{tessera_export_geotiffs()}}.
}

Coordinates are WGS84 longitude and latitude unless a spatial object
declares another CRS. Embeddings are returned on the native UTM grid of
the zone that holds them and are never resampled, except for the parts of
a \code{\link[=tessera_patch]{tessera_patch()}} that cross into another zone or onto a \code{dst_crs}.
Band indices are one-based.

Errors signalled by the package have class \code{geotessera_error}, and failed
downloads also \code{geotessera_http_error}.
}
